<title>GERMANY: German Oct/Feb sugar sales steady at 1.12 mln T.</title>
<headline>German Oct/Feb sugar sales steady at 1.12 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>German sugar sales in the first five months of the 1996/97 (Oct/Sept) season totalled 1.12 million tonnes, rounded, the same figure as in the Oct/Feb 95/96 period, sugar industry association WVZ data showed.</p>
<p>Sugar sales in February of 211,669 tonnes compared with 209,061 tonnes in February 1996.</p>
<p>Sugar production in February was 1,585 tonnes (1,714) after output peaked during the Oct/Jan beet campaign.</p>
<p>Stocks at the end of February were 2.59 million tonnes versus 2.30 million a year earlier. Carry-in stocks on Oct 1, 1996 were 239,562 tonnes (250,854 a year earlier).</p>
<p>February imports of 5,428 tonnes were down from 6,389 tonnes a year earlier while exports of 113,489 compared with 83,169 in February 1996.</p>
<p>Cumulative details (in tonnes) --</p>
<p>					    Oct/Feb 96/97  Oct/Feb 95/96</p>
<p>    Domestic sugar output	     4,180,737	3,807,136</p>
<p>    Imports				    33,053	   53,259</p>
<p>    Exports				   735,910	  693,546</p>
<p>    Domestic sales			1,123,459	1,121,078</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
